From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WayZer <himc.wicp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:52:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] FIX.G(Effect) content JSON no longer sets the initialized
 latch

Effect.initialized is a runtime latch that create() sets before init()
runs. Arc's Json#getFields exposes every declared non-transient field,
so content definitions dumped from an already created effect carry
"initialized": true. readFields() then sets the latch on a freshly
constructed effect, create() skips init(), and the interp fields
(colorInterp was added in #11477) stay at their defaults - crashing
ParticleEffect#render once the effect is finally spawned.

Marking the field transient keeps it out of JSON (Json#getFields skips
transient fields) while leaving runtime behavior unchanged; the stray
"initialized" field is now reported as unknown and ignored.
---
 core/src/mindustry/entities/Effect.java | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/src/mindustry/entities/Effect.java b/core/src/mindustry/entities/Effect.java
index 341ca42edb3cdadba7cfe6fbb8a9b5e83a2f39c4..917fa452a8f33371cba9cea6cac6cdf11c7b838f 100644
--- a/core/src/mindustry/entities/Effect.java
+++ b/core/src/mindustry/entities/Effect.java
@@ -24,7 +24,8 @@ public class Effect{
 
     public static final Seq<Effect> all = new Seq<>();
 
-    private boolean initialized;
+    //MDTX: transient, so content JSON dumps cannot set this latch and make create() skip init()
+    private transient boolean initialized;
 
     public final int id;
 
